Key translation decisions:
- Since SPX_N=16 < 24, all blakeX aliases resolve to blake256 (matching the C #if SPX_N >= 24 preprocessor logic)
- SPX_BLAKE512=0, so thash only uses the blake256 path (no 512 branch)
- The C ROUND macro in blake256/512 compress was translated to a loop over the sigma permutation table with a g256!/g512! macro that performs the same G function operations in the same order
- All wrapping arithmetic uses .wrapping_add() / .wrapping_sub() to match C unsigned overflow
- SpxCtx is #[repr(C)] with the same layout as the C struct (no SHA2/Haraka fields since this is blake)
- Exported symbols use SPX_ prefix matching the C SPX_NAMESPACE macro✓ Created checkpoint 1



